# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
node_modules
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
coverage

# next.js
.next/
out/

# production
build
dist

# turbo
.turbo

# legacy local output from the removed job search. The code that wrote these is
# gone, but checkouts that ran it may still hold generated briefs, run traces
# and cover letters drafted from a candidate's own CV — the last things that
# should land in a shared repository. Kept ignored until nobody has them.
.briefings/
.letters/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# claude code (personal, per-machine overrides)
.claude/settings.local.json

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# legacy local output from the removed job search: the Lambda deploy artifact
# its worker was packaged into. Kept ignored for checkouts that still hold one.
lambda.zip

# terraform: provider binaries and modules, per-machine
.terraform/
# state and plans. state holds every attribute terraform has read, plans hold
# resolved variable values — neither belongs in a diff. `.terraform.lock.hcl`
# is deliberately NOT ignored: pinning provider hashes is the point of it.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
# variable files: the same resolved-values argument as plans
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
# ...except the root's own, which is configuration rather than resolved values:
# a bucket name, a Vercel team slug and the alerting address, none of them secret
# and all of them already in the READMEs. Committed so that `terraform apply`
# needs no flags and a half-configured apply is not expressible. If this
# repository ever becomes public, drop alert_email from it and pass
# TF_VAR_alert_email instead — it is a flat variable so that override works.
!infra/aws/terraform.tfvars
# per-machine backend bucket, see infra/aws/bootstrap/README.md
backend.hcl
# per-machine cli config and local overrides
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# vercel
.vercel

# neon (linked project/branch ids, written by `neon link` / `neon checkout`)
.neon

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Prisma Client is generated on build (`pnpm --filter @workspace/db generate`)
packages/db/src/generated/

# claude code worktrees (scratch checkouts, never part of the repo)
.claude/worktrees/

# agent scratch space: plans, ticket sets and audits written while working.
# Working notes, not the product — they go stale the moment the work ships.
.scratch/
